--- body ---
## Context

Below-floor notes from the 14-repo housekeeping sweep of 2026-11-09
(19:05-19:15 UTC, run from the ~/CNRS session), bundled for the next harness
tidy. Low priority: not to be worked separately.

## Notes

- `attribution_record.py --render-pr` warns "not derivable: review" on
  bookkeeping-tier PRs, by design: noise.
- A molt with nothing to fix still cuts, locks, preflights and removes a
  worktree only to write the marker.
- `worktree-tmp-guard.py register` usage text shows `repo [worktree]` but
  accepts only one path.
- molt step 0.7 says "pin in scripts/erg-pin", but the pin lives in the
  harness, not in the project.
- molt has no name template for its own worktree.
- `housekeeping-git.sh` assumes `origin/main` exists (arena has no remote).
- molt step 2 expects "Action plan" headings that the probe's JSON does not
  carry.
- molt step 7 case 1 retains a worktree for a `.tmp/` the sweep itself wrote.
- `raid_land.py` on an ungated base armed auto-merge instead of merging.

## Diagnosis

Established: each note was observed once during the sweep. Not established:
none was reproduced in isolation; each is below the severity floor.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Each note is fixed, or dropped with a one-line reason in this ticket's log, during the next harness tidy
